From 7960c8a734557810afd0ee08f5e36dc877cba3a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AyhamJo7 <ayhamjumran7@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 00:05:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(control-plane): let sessions merge after an automated
 review

Founder-approved autonomy change: a session may squash-merge a PR once CI is verified on the head SHA and an independent review, which the merge gate runs itself on that exact SHA, ends in approval. No second account is needed and a session cannot supply the approval. Control-plane, CI and gate-script paths stay founder-merged permanently; migrations, identity-access, billing, usage-ledger, tool-guard and webhook paths stay founder-merged until 2026-11-29. Also narrows the attribution pattern so repository paths are no longer refused, and allows dispatching CI workflows.
